  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What each box in the middle lane is",
      "items": [
        "Lease check \u2014 has this run any steps, seconds and money left?",
        "Refresh \u00b7 resolve \u2014 recompute the registry, then find which port owns this id",
        "Inputs \u2014 turn bindings into JSON, following references to earlier steps' handles",
        "Judge \u2014 hand the effect profile to governance and wait for the answer",
        "Invoke \u2014 the component actually runs",
        "Observe \u2014 store the output under a handle and emit the events"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "How to read the other lanes",
      "items": [
        "Read the middle lane left to right \u2014 that is the step, in order",
        "Then read down from each box: the bottom lane is what the agent sees and can work around",
        "Then read up: the top lane is the run ending, not a value anyone receives",
        "Governance's own lane holds Ask, the one answer that neither proceeds nor stops"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two error classes, on purpose",
      "items": [
        "A component that raises, an unknown id, and a binding to nothing are all data \u2014 a Failed observation the agent can read and route around",
        "A port that raises is a failure \u2014 your host is broken, and the run ends rather than reasoning past it",
        "Refuse is neither: it is a decision, recorded, with the component never called"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ask is not a rejection",
      "items": [
        "Ask parks the run on a checkpoint and yields an Asked event to you",
        "The answer may come back seconds later, or from a different process entirely",
        "A slow human, a long job and a sub-agent all use this same mechanism"
      ]
    }
  ]
